.TH "GF-ORGS-ADD-ORG-USER" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-orgs-add-org-user - Adds a new user to the current organization


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf orgs add-org-user [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a global user to the current organization.

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled you need to have a permission with action: \fBorg.users:add\fR with scope \fBusers:*\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (AddOrgUserCommand):
{
  "loginOrEmail": string,
  "role": string
}
  role                     enum: None | Viewer | Editor | Admin


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	The path to the body json file or json string. For example, --body=/path/to/body.json or --body='{"foo": "bar"}'

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add-org-user

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	OrgID


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-orgs(1)\fP
